  "title": "Where City Efficiency Improves in Everyday Interactions",
  "summary": "For residents, getting a permit, paying a bill, or accessing a record often involves more effort than it should. A single request can trigger follow-up calls, status checks, or repeated data entry across multiple systems. What appears to be a routine task becomes a series of interactions between residents, staff, and disconnected processes. Those interactions create operational strain over time. As service demand grows, staff workload grows with it — not always because the work itself...",
